 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 519085,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Brian consolidates his federal student loans into one loan at 4.99%. The consolidated balance is $20,340, and he extends the term to 12 years. What are Brian’s monthly payments for the consolidated loan?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The standard plan is 12 payments a year for 10 years.</p>\n<p>To compute the payment to pay down a loan with beginning principal, <i>P</i>, the payment (<i>pmt</i>) is <span data-math=\"pmt = \\frac{{P \\times \\frac{r}{n} \\times {{\\left( {1 + \\frac{r}{n}} \\right)}^{n \\times t}}}}{{{{\\left( {1 + \\frac{r}{n}} \\right)}^{n \\times t}} - 1}}\"></span>, where <i>r</i> is the annual interest rate (in decimal form), <i>n</i> is the number of compounding periods per year, and <i>t</i> is the number of years. Note, payment to lenders is always rounded up to the next penny.</p>\n<p>If the number of periods per year is 1, then the formula is simplified to <span data-math=\"pmt = \\frac{{P \\times r \\times {{\\left( {1 + r} \\right)}^t}}}{{{{\\left( {1 + r} \\right)}^t} - 1}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>Once again, it will help you get the right answer from your calculator to find <span data-math=\"n \\times t\"></span> first.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"n \\times t = \\left( {12} \\right)\\left( {12} \\right) = 144\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"pmt = \\frac{{\\left( {20,340 \\times \\frac{{0.0499}}{{12}} \\times {{\\left( {1 + \\frac{{0.0499}}{{12}}} \\right)}^{144}}} \\right)}}{{\\left( {{{\\left( {1 + \\frac{{0.0499}}{{12}}} \\right)}^{144}} - 1} \\right)}} = \\$188.03\"></span></p>\n<p>Additional parentheses were added to help you enter the expression properly in your calculator.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$188.03"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
